@startuml
title Operator-driven physical database registration

participant "Kubernetes API" as K8s
participant "DBaaS Operator" as Operator
participant "DBaaS Adapter" as Adapter
participant "DBaaS Aggregator" as Aggregator
database "DBaaS Registry" as Registry

K8s -> Operator: reconcile PhysicalDatabaseRegistration\n(created, spec changed, refresh annotation, or periodic re-sync)

opt spec.operatorNamespace belongs to another operator instance
  Operator --> K8s: skip the resource, write no status
end

opt another PhysicalDatabaseRegistration claims the same\nphysicalDatabaseId or the same adapter.address
  Operator -> K8s: phase InvalidConfiguration, Ready=False, Stalled=True (RegistrationConflict);\nstop the reconcile
  note right of Operator
    The older claimant wins, by creationTimestamp and then by UID.
  end note
end

Operator -> K8s: read the adapter credentials Secret\n(spec.adapter.credentialsSecretRef)
K8s --> Operator: user name and password, or error
opt Secret is absent, a key is missing or empty, or RBAC denies the read
  Operator -> K8s: phase BackingOff, Ready=False, Stalled=False (SecretError);\nstop the reconcile
end

Operator -> Adapter: check which physical database the adapter serves\nGET {adapter.address}/api/v2/dbaas/adapter/{type}/physical_database
Adapter --> Operator: served physical database id, or error
note right of Operator
  The operator sends status "running", so the aggregator skips
  its own handshake. This probe takes the place of it.
end note

opt probe did not answer 200 with the expected physical database id
  alt adapter is unreachable, or answers a status other than 200, 401 or 403
    Operator -> K8s: phase BackingOff, Ready=False, Stalled=False (AdapterUnavailable);\nstop the reconcile
  else adapter answers 401 or 403
    Operator -> K8s: phase BackingOff, Ready=False, Stalled=False (AdapterUnauthorized);\nstop the reconcile
  else adapter answers with another physical database id
    Operator -> K8s: phase InvalidConfiguration, Ready=False, Stalled=True (AdapterIdentityMismatch);\nstop the reconcile
  end
end

Operator -> Aggregator: register physical database\nPUT /api/v3/dbaas/{type}/physical_databases/{phydbid}\n(adapter address, credentials, supported roles, features,\nstatus "running", API version v2)
ref over Aggregator, Registry: Physical database registration

alt 201 Created, or 200 OK
  Aggregator --> Operator: physical database registered, or already up to date
  Operator -> K8s: phase Succeeded, Ready=True, Stalled=False (AdapterRegistered)

else 202 Accepted
  Aggregator --> Operator: instruction id and the first portion of logical databases\nthat need users for the new roles
  Operator -> K8s: phase WaitingForDependency, Ready=False, Stalled=False (RoleMigrationStarted);\nstore the instruction id and the migration generation
  ref over Operator, Registry: Operator-driven additional roles migration
  note right of Operator
    Nothing is written to the physical database on this path.
    The registration request stays parked in the migration plan
    until the migration completes.
  end note

else 400 Bad Request, 403 Forbidden, or 409 Conflict
  Aggregator --> Operator: the request conflicts with a registration, or is malformed
  Operator -> K8s: phase InvalidConfiguration, Ready=False, Stalled=True (AggregatorRejected)

else 401 Unauthorized
  Aggregator --> Operator: operator credentials are rejected
  Operator -> K8s: phase BackingOff, Ready=False, Stalled=False (Unauthorized)

else 500 Internal Server Error, network failure, or timeout
  Aggregator --> Operator: the request failed
  Operator -> K8s: phase BackingOff, Ready=False, Stalled=False (AggregatorError)
end

Operator -> K8s: requeue after the re-sync interval

legend bottom right
  Solid arrow: synchronous request. Dashed arrow: response.
  Every step runs inside one reconcile of the custom resource.
  Every status line reads: phase, conditions, (Reason).
  The aggregator's own branch logic is drawn in Physical database registration.
endlegend
@enduml

